{"index":2227,"node_id":"cc8216ab-a224-4a04-95b0-58bece9b43bd","parent":"881aeae4-9985-4666-8375-fb880110257d","role":"assistant","author_name":null,"create_time":1791099453.131701,"update_time":1791100852.805485,"content_type":"text","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":true,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"Not directly as a GitHub Actions `workflow_dispatch` input through the connector I have here. There is no exposed dispatch action in my current GitHub toolset.\n\nWhat I **can** do directly is:\n\n- create/update a file on a branch,\n- create a branch,\n- open a PR,\n- label the PR,\n- and thereby trigger a workflow that listens to `push`, `pull_request`, or `pull_request_target`.\n\nSo for your setup, the clean pattern is:\n\n```text\nI write input file to processing/<run-id>\n→ commit happens\n→ open PR / add required label\n→ PR workflow fires\n→ workflow reads the input from the branch\n```\n\nIf you want true parameter-style inputs without committing a file, that would require an exposed `workflow_dispatch`/`repository_dispatch` action or some other API path I don't currently have in this connector."}
